---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import ButtonLink from "../components/ButtonLink.astro";
import CommandBlock from "../components/CommandBlock.astro";
import { RELEASE, SITE } from "../data/site";

const curlCommand = `curl -fLO \\
  '${RELEASE.baseUrl}/{SHA256SUMS,${RELEASE.archive}}'`;
const installCommand = `tar -xf ${RELEASE.archive} &&
cd ${RELEASE.archive.replace(".tar.xz", "")} &&
sudo install -Dm755 suzumushi /usr/local/bin/suzumushi &&
sudo ln -s suzumushi /usr/local/bin/suzu`;
---

<Layout title="Install" description="Install Suzumushi on Linux and set up your first local audio library.">
  <section class="section shell pb-8">
    <p class="eyebrow">Linux release · v{SITE.version}</p>
    <h1 class="page-title mt-4">Install Suzumushi.</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-muted">Choose the AUR package for Arch Linux or the archive for x86-64 GNU/Linux. Then create your library below.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="shell pb-14 sm:pb-16" aria-label="Installation options">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 items-start gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <article class="panel p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="section-title">Arch Linux</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">Install the AUR package with yay. Both <code class="font-mono text-sm text-ink">suzumushi</code> and <code class="font-mono text-sm text-ink">suzu</code> launch the player.</p>
        <div class="mt-6"><CommandBlock command="yay -S suzumushi-bin" label="Install with yay" /></div>
        <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-5">
          <a class="text-link" href="#first-library">Next: set up your library →</a>
          <a class="text-link text-sm" href={SITE.aur} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">AUR package ↗</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="panel p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="section-title">GNU/Linux x86-64</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">Download the release archive, verify its checksum, and install the player.</p>
        <details class="mt-6">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer py-2 font-medium text-ink">Show archive installation steps</summary>
          <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6">
            <CommandBlock command={curlCommand} label="1. Download" />
            <div>
              <CommandBlock command="sha256sum --check --ignore-missing SHA256SUMS" label="2. Verify" />
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">Continue only if the archive reports <code class="font-mono text-ink">OK</code>. If verification fails, stop and download the files again.</p>
            </div>
            <CommandBlock command={installCommand} label="3. Install" />
            <details>
              <summary class="cursor-pointer py-2 text-sm text-muted">Expected SHA-256 for v{SITE.version}</summary>
              <p class="mt-3 break-all font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink">{RELEASE.checksum}</p>
            </details>
            <a class="text-link" href="#first-library">Next: set up your library →</a>
          </div>
        </details>
        <a class="text-link mt-6 inline-block text-sm" href={SITE.release} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Release files ↗</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="first-library" class="border-y border-line bg-panel/40" aria-labelledby="first-library-title">
    <div class="section shell grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[0.85fr_1.15fr] lg:gap-16">
      <div>
        <h2 id="first-library-title" class="section-title">Set up your first library.</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">Run these commands from the folder where you want to keep your Suzumushi library. The player reads audio inside that library; it doesn't automatically scan your Music folder.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="setup-steps">
        <li>
          <h3 class="mb-3 font-semibold">Create a Suzumushi folder</h3>
          <CommandBlock command="suzumushi init ./suzumushi" label="Create library" />
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3 class="font-semibold">Add your music</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-muted">In your file manager, copy audio files or folders into <code>./suzumushi/audio/library/</code>. You can keep your artist and album folders.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3 class="mb-3 font-semibold">Open the player</h3>
          <CommandBlock command="suzumushi --root ./suzumushi" label="Start listening" />
          <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">Select a track in Library and press <kbd>Enter</kbd> to add it and start playback. Use <kbd>Space</kbd> to pause and <kbd>?</kbd> for the key guide.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell">
    <div class="prose max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="!mt-0">Audio support</h2>
      <p>The verified formats are MP3, FLAC, signed 16-bit PCM WAV, and Ogg Vorbis. Mono and stereo audio from 8 kHz through 192 kHz is supported when the default device accepts the source rate.</p>
      <p>AAC, M4A, Opus, multichannel audio, and automatic resampling are not included in verified support.</p>

      <details class="mt-8 border-t border-line pt-4">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer py-2 font-semibold text-ink">Build from source</summary>
        <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-1 gap-5">
          <p>You need Rust 1.95 or newer and the development packages for your distribution.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Arch Linux: <code>alsa-lib dbus pipewire clang pkgconf</code></li>
            <li>Debian or Ubuntu: <code>libasound2-dev libpipewire-0.3-dev libspa-0.2-dev libdbus-1-dev libclang-dev pkg-config</code></li>
            <li>Fedora: <code>alsa-lib-devel pipewire-devel dbus-devel libclang-devel pkgconf-pkg-config</code></li>
          </ul>
          <CommandBlock command={`git clone https://github.com/nuggocto/suzumushi.git &&\ncd suzumushi &&\ncargo install --path . --locked`} label="Build and install" />
          <p>After installation, follow the <a href="#first-library">library setup instructions</a> above.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
    <ButtonLink href="/" variant="secondary" class="mt-8">Back to the player</ButtonLink>
  </section>
</Layout>
